> tl;dr
>
> - Established a living risk register to steer prioritization and mitigation.
> - Adopted predictable 3‑week release cycles; increased release quality and stakeholder confidence.
> - Required measurable outcomes per major ticket to align work with organizational goals.
> - Impact sustained through cross‑team collaboration and disciplined leadership practices.

We had delivery energy but couldn't predict what would ship when. Stakeholders asked "when will X be ready?" and we couldn't answer confidently. We needed a way to steer work toward the highest‑value outcomes while managing new platform risk.

A living risk register, predictable 3‑week cadence, and explicit outcomes on every significant ticket gave us that steering mechanism. Stakeholders got clearer expectations; the team got focus.

## Problem

Stakeholders needed predictability and evidence that delivery aligned to strategic objectives while managing new platform risks.

## Approach

- Built a concise risk register with owners, triggers, and mitigations.
- Moved to a 3‑week cadence with scope control and demo checkpoints.
- Defined outcome templates for major tickets (metrics, audience, value).

## Outcomes

- Predictable releases with clear change notes and demo acceptance.
- Backlog aligned to risk/impact rather than convenience ordering.
- Higher signal in reporting: tie work artifacts to measurable outcomes.
- Release cadence maintained at ~3 weeks throughout 2024-2025.
- 90%+ of major tickets include defined outcomes and success metrics.
- Risk register reviewed each cycle with owner sign-off and mitigation tracking.
